From 63e59819d43688def38ff0df67440a4aecb88d9c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 5 Aug 2026 13:46:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Redraw the strategic map to June 1926
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Rename 武漢 to 漢口 and 瀋陽 to 奉天; drop 海東, 臨夏 and 韶關, none of which
existed under those names in June 1926.

Replace the rectangular province boxes with real polygon boundaries for the
24 units of June 1926 that the game map actually covers, generated by
scripts/build_provinces_1926.py and clipped to the CHINA_PROPER silhouette in
frontend/map.js, so the boundary set can never drift outside the playable area.
青海 and 寧夏 fold back into 甘肅, which they were part of at the time. 綏遠,
察哈爾 and 熱河 are kept as provinces. Areas administratively carved out of a
province -- 膠澳商埠, 東省特別區, 川邊, 京兆 -- are not modelled; those cells
resolve to the surrounding province. 直隸/熱河/察哈爾, 奉天/熱河 and 吉林/黑龍江
now follow their historical lines rather than lon/lat boxes.

The map now has exactly one source. frontend/data/provinces_1926.geojson is
what app.js fetches; the generator's input moves to scripts/data/ so nothing
served can be mistaken for the live map. Six unreferenced files that carried
their own outdated copies of the map -- map_config.js, map_renderer.js,
china_map.js, china_map_data.js, china_map.html and map_data.html -- are
removed.

Mark the ten treaty-port concessions as a city property that does not affect
sovereignty or capture and carries no foreign garrison, and classify every
city as river port, sea port, both or inland. Concessions pay +1 cash and
+1 factory every third turn, river ports +1 cash, sea ports +2 cash; the
bonuses stack and are not scaled by ECONOMY_SCALE.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CaTX3RKA2kKdVQcg1D4C4M
